{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 37, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the morning sun unusually bright. He stretched, feeling…different. Not physically, but like something was *off*. The familiar creak of his old bed frame sounded strangely amplified, almost echoing. He glanced at his reflection in the dusty mirror – the same tired face, the same thinning hair – but something felt…hollow. He reached for his glasses, and as his fingers brushed against the plastic, a jolt of static electricity shot up his arm. Then, the room shimmered. The peeling wallpaper, the mismatched furniture, the slightly lopsided lampshade – all sharpened, became hyper-real, with edges that seemed to pulse. A notification popped into his vision: \"Level Up: Arthur. Current Status: Civilian. Objective: Survive.\" Panic seized him. He stumbled out of bed, tripping over a discarded sock. The sock, impossibly, seemed to *move* as he reached for it, a tiny, animated creature. This wasn't his life.\n\n***\n\nHe bolted out the door, the familiar suburban street transforming into a vibrant, blocky landscape. The houses were rendered in perfect, pixelated detail, the trees impossibly green and swaying with a wind that felt…programmed. A squirrel, rendered with unnerving realism, chattered at him, then scampered up a tree with a speed that defied physics. Arthur ran, heart pounding, desperately trying to understand. He saw other people, all dressed in generic, brightly colored outfits, moving with a rigid, almost unnatural grace. They weren’t interacting, just following pre-determined paths. A voice, crisp and synthesized, echoed in his mind: \"Warning: Player detected. Initiating Tutorial Sequence.\" Arthur knew, with a chilling certainty, that he wasn't just living in a simulation. He was *in* one. And the game had just begun.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.7354406118392944}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -1.50833